📊 Bike Sales Dashboard Insights
Project Overview

This dashboard analyzes 1,283 bike sales records across multiple Indian states and brands. It provides insights into bike pricing, resale value, mileage, fuel type distribution, and manufacturing trends, helping understand customer preferences and market performance.

📈 Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)
Metric	Value
Total Bikes	1,283
Average Selling Price	₹224,329
Average Resale Price	₹133,829
Average Mileage	67.19 km/l (Expected)
Insight
The dataset contains 1,283 bike listings, providing a reliable sample for analysis.
Bikes retain approximately 60% of their original selling price on average.
The average selling price indicates a market focused on mid-range premium motorcycles.
🔹 Brand Performance
Insight
Kawasaki has the highest number of listed bikes, indicating strong availability in the dataset.
Yamaha, KTM, and Royal Enfield also have high listing volumes, showing strong market presence.
Honda and Bajaj have comparatively fewer listings.
Business Insight

High listing volume may indicate strong customer demand or a larger second-hand market for these brands.

💰 Average Price by Brand
Insight
Bajaj has the highest average selling price in this dataset.
Hero and Yamaha also maintain competitive average prices.
Honda has the lowest average selling price among the major brands.
Business Insight

Premium pricing does not necessarily depend on brand popularity; it is also influenced by model type, manufacturing year, and engine capacity.

